 "not_verified": [
  "The forms of D78.15 (2): a window count, min or max of a Float, count() over a window with no partition or order key (with or without a frame), and the INTEGER minimum written as one signed literal. PostgreSQL project mode refuses them, so they have native cells only, which the owner ruled enough to open them (D78.16).",
  "The results one past the bounds: the premise controls (a +, a binary and a unary -, a * and a sum of squares past signed 64 bits give a REAL in SQLite) and the cells arith-square-over, arith-abs-of-the-minimum, window-sum-over and window-sum-under (integer overflow); PostgreSQL's SQLSTATE 22003 there stays inferred.",
  "A sum, grouped or over a window, under a limit without an order by whose overflow lies in a group or partial sum that no delivered row needs: whether such a statement fails is not compared, and no cell has that shape."
 ],
